        "title": "fix(google-meet): use truncateUtf16Safe for log value truncation",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nOne `.slice(0, 180)` truncation site in the Google Meet extension may cut UTF-16 surrogate pairs in half when the log value contains multi-byte characters such as emoji.\n\n## Changes\n\n- `extensions/google-meet/src/realtime.ts`: replace `value?.replace(...).slice(0, 180)` with `truncateUtf16Safe`.\n\nLabel: bugfix | merge-risk: 🟢 minimal",
